1
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:19,770
<i>Why?</i>

2
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:25,400
<i>Why am I on my knees without scoring a single goal?</i>

3
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:28,940
<i>I was supposed to be the king of the field.</i>

4
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,450
<i>I,</i>

5
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:35,990
<i>was always the leader on the field.</i>

6
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:40,660
You're amazing, Barou-kun.

7
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,250
<i>I'm talented.</i>

8
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:47,250
I'm so happy to be on the same team as Barou!

9
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,960
<i>Everyone besides me is an extra.</i>

10
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:56,470
All of you, play for me to score.

11
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:57,720
Understood!

12
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,220
We're invincible now!

13
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:03,060
<i>These brats are so happy even though they're just extras.</i>

14
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:05,480
<i>What do they enjoy about soccer?</i>

15
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,610
I am the king.

16
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:13,780
<i>I gave up trying to understand others</i>

17
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:17,240
<i>and decided to continue with my own soccer.</i>

18
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:19,950
<i>And so I realized this.</i>

19
00:01:20,030 --> 00:01:26,080
<i>I don't love soccer because I get to taste the feeling of being king</i>

20
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:30,670
<i>or because I enjoy running around the field.</i>

21
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:34,420
<i>It's just that I love</i>

22
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:37,510
<i>knocking off the stage with my own goal</i>

23
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:39,890
<i>those who, like me,</i>

24
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:41,930
<i>have dedicated their lives to soccer.</i>

25
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:47,350
<i>I play soccer to taste this feeling.</i>

26
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:53,820
<i>What I know better than anyone</i>

27
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:58,780
<i>is that this feeling is a unique pleasure</i>

28
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,490
<i>that only the strongest can taste.</i>

29
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:37,380
If they score one more, we lose, Isagi.

30
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,420
Let's score while we have the ball.

31
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:41,380
Got it. That way we can catch up—

32
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:46,100
Go on!

33
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:49,230
- Seriously?
- Did he shoot directly?

34
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,020
Shit!

35
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,770
Kunigami, loose ball!

36
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:54,860
Okay!

37
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,070
We're going, Reo! Direct counter—

38
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:01,030
Try it if you can, blockhead.

39
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,280
<i>This guy makes quick decisions!</i>

40
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:07,620
I'm here, Kunigami! If you lose it in front of the goal, we're screwed!

41
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:09,120
Nice! To you, Reo!

42
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,790
What?

43
00:04:12,830 --> 00:04:14,380
<i>Did he read my move?</i>

44
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,670
<i>I won't let you</i>

45
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:19,380
<i>do as you please any more!</i>

46
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:21,550
Loose ball.

47
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,260
<i>It's finally here.</i>

48
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,890
<i>The big chance for me to shine.</i>

49
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,890
<i>My shooting range is wide open.</i>

50
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,520
<i>If I can advance 2-3 meters with one touch,</i>

51
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,320
<i>I can score a guaranteed goal!</i>

52
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,940
You're one step behind, king.

53
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:44,410
I'm faster than you.

54
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:45,910
<i>You little shit.</i>

55
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:48,870
<i>He'll catch me with just one touch!</i>

56
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:50,830
<i>Screw this!</i>

57
00:04:50,910 --> 00:04:54,290
<i>What should I do? Should I shoot? But I'm out of range.</i>

58
00:04:54,370 --> 00:04:56,000
<i>Shit!</i>

59
00:04:56,670 --> 00:04:59,000
<i>Even though my zone is right in front of me!</i>

60
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:00,880
<i>I'm one step</i>

61
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:03,630
<i>short.</i>

62
00:05:11,350 --> 00:05:14,060
<i>Pass it to me.</i>

63
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,340
Nice pass, loser.

64
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:52,890
Play for my goal.

65
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:58,270
<i>What is this...</i>

66
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:08,700
<i>despair that's gripping my heart?</i>

67
00:06:09,990 --> 00:06:13,080
<i>Is this what they call 'defeat'?</i>

68
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:18,040
<i>I didn't want to make that pass,</i>

69
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,420
<i>I was forced to make it.</i>

70
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:25,800
<i>In that moment, I lost to Yoichi Isagi.</i>

71
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,590
Get out of my way.

72
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:32,180
Or I'll kill you.

73
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:34,890
You're talentless.

74
00:06:34,970 --> 00:06:39,020
As the king, shall I personally crush you?

75
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,690
Go to sleep, you mediocre piece of trash.

76
00:06:40,770 --> 00:06:43,480
<i>I decide for myself what I'm going to do.</i>

77
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:47,570
I'd rather die than play for someone else.

78
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,450
Play for my goal.

79
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:54,870
<i>He was no longer the protagonist, and</i>

80
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:58,750
<i>soccer was no longer serving me.</i>

81
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,920
<i>I wasn't the king.</i>

82
00:07:09,590 --> 00:07:11,840
Isagi is in terrible shape right now.

83
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:14,300
So the next kickoff is the last.

84
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:17,100
No matter what, don't let the ball reach Isagi.

85
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:20,310
Exactly. If he gets it, I don't think we can stop him.

86
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:24,150
The last kickoff is ours.

87
00:07:24,230 --> 00:07:26,360
We'll definitely score and win.

88
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,280
Consider it a loss the moment we lose the ball.

89
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:31,860
Then let's use my speed.

90
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:35,620
I'm the best option we have.

91
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:38,700
Alright, we'll move according to you.

92
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:42,670
If we're betting everything on the final shot, this is the best.

93
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:44,960
We'll definitely win.

94
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,000
That's right.

95
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:47,920
No need for the rest.

96
00:07:50,010 --> 00:07:52,050
The kickoff is theirs.

97
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:55,350
Unless we can get the ball, there's no point in talking.

98
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:56,640
Okay.

99
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:59,100
But the biggest problem is Chigiri.

100
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:03,850
<i>Even if we mark him, he can outrun us by dashing.</i>

101
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:07,520
<i>Also, if he controls it like he did earlier, he won't even slow down.</i>

102
00:08:07,610 --> 00:08:09,820
If we start running at the same time,

103
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:11,780
there's no way we can win.

104
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,280
In that case,

105
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:17,240
let's stop him before he runs.

106
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,540
Did you think of something?

107
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,330
Yeah, I'll take Reo—

108
00:08:21,410 --> 00:08:22,830
Wait a minute.

109
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,460
Aren't we going to share it with him?

110
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:31,470
It's easier for the three of us to defend, and if they score this, we lose.

111
00:08:32,630 --> 00:08:34,970
It's no use talking to the fallen king.

112
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:40,470
You and I will decide the fate of the last kickoff.

113
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:41,930
As you command.

114
00:08:49,730 --> 00:08:53,400
<i>They're concentrated on not letting me pass to Chigiri.</i>

115
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,990
<i>Meanwhile, Kunigami is wide open in the middle.</i>

116
00:08:57,700 --> 00:09:00,240
<i>So, they don't care if I pass to him?</i>

117
00:09:00,330 --> 00:09:03,330
<i>Shit. Even if I want to use Chigiri's speed,</i>

118
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:06,710
<i>I can't make anything more than useless passes this way.</i>

119
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:10,000
<i>Also, Nagi is holding Chigiri to the death.</i>

120
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:13,380
<i>They've mastered every scrap of our tactics.</i>

121
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,430
Kunigami!

122
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:16,930
<i>They're underestimating me.</i>

123
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:18,390
<i>But what am I going to do?</i>

124
00:09:18,470 --> 00:09:20,640
<i>A random pass is too risky.</i>

125
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,810
<i>Should I try to dodge Barou?</i>

126
00:09:22,890 --> 00:09:25,270
<i>No, too risky.</i>

127
00:09:25,350 --> 00:09:26,690
Reo, one more time!

128
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:29,770
<i>It's not working. We can't get anywhere with just Kunigami.</i>

129
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:32,400
<i>Besides, what am I even thinking?</i>

130
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,990
<i>I just need to beat this!</i>

131
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:35,820
<i>I'll open the path</i>

132
00:09:36,490 --> 00:09:38,240
<i>to Chigiri myself!</i>

133
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,490
<i>Not yet.</i>

134
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:41,990
<i>Wait for it to come.</i>

135
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,370
<i>I don't need to get past him.</i>

136
00:09:43,450 --> 00:09:45,660
<i>It's enough if a path opens for the pass.</i>

137
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:47,370
<i>Just a moment is enough!</i>

138
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:50,960
<i>I see it!</i>

139
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:53,710
Run!

140
00:09:56,050 --> 00:09:59,180
<i>Victory is mine, Yoichi Isagi!</i>

141
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,890
<i>Leave the rest to me!</i>

142
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:04,810
<i>This kid,</i>

143
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:06,520
<i>where is he going?</i>

144
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:08,980
<i>He's running towards my pass.</i>

145
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,520
<i>Don't tell me,</i>

146
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:15,240
<i>because he knows he can't win against Chigiri, he's going for broke and</i>

147
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,740
<i>will take my pass directly?</i>

148
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,200
Nice pass, Reo.

149
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,450
We were waiting for this.

150
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,330
<i>Is this a joke?</i>

151
00:10:26,410 --> 00:10:29,920
<i>Was all of this his plan?</i>

152
00:10:30,670 --> 00:10:34,800
<i>If he hadn't reached it, Chigiri would have gotten the ball and the game would be over.</i>

153
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:36,760
<i>Reach it.</i>

154
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:45,850
<i>They took a huge gamble in the last minute of the match.</i>

155
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,940
Phew. That was close.

156
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,690
Loose ball!

157
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:58,950
We're going, loser.

158
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:03,080
Bring it on, king!

159
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,450
<i>Once I accepted defeat,</i>

160
00:11:07,450 --> 00:11:13,000
<i>the whole field seemed to shine for his goal.</i>

161
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:17,800
<i>Despite that, the reason I'm not frustrated</i>

162
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:20,720
<i>might be because I'm no longer the protagonist.</i>

163
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,180
I'm here!

164
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,640
I'm here too!

165
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,350
<i>This guy,</i>

166
00:11:25,430 --> 00:11:26,810
Wait!

167
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:30,190
I won't let you do as you please, genius!

168
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:32,690
You again, troublesome princess?

169
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,230
<i>This is the first time I'm tasting these feelings.</i>

170
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:40,490
<i>They're annoying me by showing me the paths to the goal.</i>

171
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,280
<i>As an extra now,</i>

172
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:44,700
<i>if I pass, we can win.</i>

173
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:47,620
<i>I could become a part of the goal.</i>

174
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:52,250
<i>Right now, compared to me, you are shining brightly.</i>

175
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:56,920
<i>Shit. So it was something like this.</i>

176
00:11:57,630 --> 00:12:01,680
<i>So the extras who passed to me until now</i>

177
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,590
<i>felt like this.</i>

178
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:09,810
<i>This feeling of defeat can only be overcome</i>

179
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:13,560
<i>by entrusting the goal to a superior striker!</i>

180
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,440
<i>We can win with my pass.</i>

181
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,910
<i>So this is what they call a 'team'.</i>

182
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,450
<i>This is what they call a 'chemical reaction'.</i>

183
00:12:24,610 --> 00:12:26,990
<i>This is the purpose of living for a defeated extra.</i>

184
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:34,790
<i>What's going on?</i>

185
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:36,750
<i>What are these?</i>

186
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,750
<i>Is what's holding me</i>

187
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:43,470
<i>the future that awaits me after this pass?</i>

188
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,550
<i>I see.</i>

189
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:47,800
<i>Entrusting it,</i>

190
00:12:49,890 --> 00:12:53,730
<i>could save my defeated self.</i>

191
00:12:54,770 --> 00:12:58,520
<i>But this is nothing more than an excuse</i>

192
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:02,400
<i>created by those whose dreams are shattered to deny their past.</i>

193
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,320
<i>That's right.</i>

194
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,070
<i>The excuse of the defeated.</i>

195
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:12,910
<i>There's no way</i>

196
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,500
<i>I'm going to live</i>

197
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:20,710
<i>such a future!</i>

198
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:23,220
<i>A sudden maneuver?</i>

199
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,300
<i>And a 90-degree dribble at that?</i>

200
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:27,140
<i>The path I need to see...</i>

201
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,720
- Barou!
- Can he do such things?

202
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:32,390
<i>The situation is bad.</i>

203
00:13:32,470 --> 00:13:34,680
<i>If he passes to Isagi, we're done.</i>

204
00:13:34,770 --> 00:13:36,020
<i>From where?</i>

205
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:38,810
<i>Is he going to dribble past me directly?</i>

206
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:41,730
<i>No, he's definitely going to pass!</i>

207
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:45,650
<i>What? A consecutive maneuver?</i>

208
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:49,120
<i>Did he use Isagi as a decoy?</i>

209
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:52,540
<i>He's pulling off lightning-fast dribbling without losing speed!</i>

210
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,750
<i>Is this for real?</i>

211
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:59,080
<i>Did he just evolve at a time like this?</i>

212
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:01,670
Run, Chigiri! Barou isn't going to pass right now!

213
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:05,010
<i>I can see it! I can feel it!</i>

214
00:14:05,090 --> 00:14:07,970
<i>What I needed to see, because I tasted defeat,</i>

215
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:11,640
<i>isn't a path to entrust the goal to the protagonist,</i>

216
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:15,640
<i>but the shadow that exists</i>

217
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,770
<i>for my own goal!</i>

218
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:22,610
<i>Did he use Isagi to hide his next move?</i>

219
00:14:22,690 --> 00:14:25,240
<i>Hiding behind the light you created,</i>

220
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,450
<i>it's my turn to devour you!</i>

221
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:34,160
<i>These guys are devouring each other!</i>

222
00:14:35,450 --> 00:14:37,500
<i>This is Barou's awakening.</i>

223
00:14:39,290 --> 00:14:41,290
<i>Our chemical reaction,</i>

224
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,170
<i>advancing by devouring each other!</i>

225
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:46,420
So you're going to crush them all.

226
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,340
<i>I'm not going to remain an extra.</i>

227
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,220
Move!

228
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:57,480
<i>If you are the protagonist, then I am happy</i>

229
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:00,230
<i>to be the villain who devours you!</i>

230
00:15:02,810 --> 00:15:04,900
Holy shit.

231
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:07,900
Welcome back, king.

232
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:18,200
<i>This deviant path is my new way of being king.</i>

233
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:21,880
<i>The king</i>

234
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,920
<i>is me!</i>

235
00:15:34,470 --> 00:15:36,220
<i>Score, 4-5.</i>

236
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:40,850
<i>Blue Lock 2nd Selection, 3rd Stage, 3-on-3 Rivalry Battle.</i>

237
00:15:42,270 --> 00:15:43,270
Barou!

238
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,650
<i>The winner is the White Team.</i>

239
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:49,860
<i>Isagi Yoichi.</i>

240
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:52,320
- Oh, he left me hanging.
- <i>Nagi Seishiro.</i>

241
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:54,030
<i>Barou Shouei.</i>

242
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,120
First of all,

243
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,580
take it back.

244
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,080
Am I a 'loser'?

245
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:06,040
Sorry, I was mistaken.

246
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:08,800
You really are amazing!

247
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:13,430
My performance drops when I'm with you.

248
00:16:13,510 --> 00:16:14,800
It was a good shot.

249
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:18,810
We won, we won! We won!

250
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:20,890
Nagi, you...

251
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:23,100
Get off me, damn it.

252
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:26,440
Your chop dribble was beyond legendary.

253
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,230
If you had things like that, you should tell us.

254
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,280
Shut up.

255
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,240
I just discovered it too.

256
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,360
How?

257
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,410
Tell me about yourself.

258
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:44,370
Until now, I've only seen the field as my own.

259
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:47,710
It was like everything besides me was insignificant.

260
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:54,220
But you two, for the first time in my life, stole the protagonist role from me.

261
00:16:55,010 --> 00:16:58,140
<i>So, to survive here,</i>

262
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:01,980
<i>I found a way to dominate the field as the villain.</i>

263
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:04,020
That's all.

264
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:08,190
It's normal, the opponents were really strong too.

265
00:17:08,270 --> 00:17:11,400
You wouldn't taste this feeling against average opponents.

266
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,610
So, something like that.

267
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:21,120
So your new weapon, the 'chop dribble', was born like this?

268
00:17:21,830 --> 00:17:25,460
You really are amazing.

269
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:26,920
Not really.

270
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,090
Whether I'm a villain or not,

271
00:17:29,170 --> 00:17:34,260
my dream is to become the world's best striker as the king of the field.

272
00:17:36,470 --> 00:17:41,220
I will never lose to you again, Isagi.

273
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:47,770
Did you just call Isagi by his first name for the first time?

274
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:51,570
Do I have nothing better to do than remember that?

275
00:17:51,650 --> 00:17:53,610
You're a pain, Mr. Hassle.

276
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:57,450
It's not Mr. Hassle, it's 'Nagi'. Call me by my name too.

277
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,910
Shut up, you bastards.

278
00:18:00,990 --> 00:18:03,370
Look at that. Rough guy.

279
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:06,580
Nagi.

280
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:11,540
Alright.

281
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:16,090
ISAGI, NAGI, BAROU

282
00:18:17,010 --> 00:18:18,050
Wow.

283
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,890
Passing 3 people with a chop dribble

284
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:24,560
and a perfectly accurate shot to the top right corner.

285
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:28,900
Looking at his pure talent, he's one of the best in the country.

286
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,770
Barou Shouei-kun.

287
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:34,230
You calculated his awakening too, didn't you, Ego-san?

288
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:37,450
No, not at all. That's his talent.

289
00:18:37,530 --> 00:18:38,450
What?

290
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:40,030
Listen carefully, Anri-chan.

291
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:45,080
Defeat is a normal situation that inevitably occurs in the world of battle.

292
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:50,460
Even if you are the world's best striker, you cannot win every match.

293
00:18:51,170 --> 00:18:55,260
What matters is what you gain from defeat.

294
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:59,260
The defeated are rejected by the field.

295
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:02,970
For a warrior, there is no heavier despair than this.

296
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:07,850
But most mediocre people don't learn from this despair.

297
00:19:07,930 --> 00:19:09,440
This is important.

298
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:13,110
<i>Because they are pushed aside due to their weakness and lack of talent,</i>

299
00:19:13,190 --> 00:19:15,610
<i>and because they are afraid to accept their mistakes,</i>

300
00:19:15,690 --> 00:19:17,650
<i>they involuntarily make up excuses.</i>

301
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:21,240
<i>Truly 'involuntarily'.</i>

302
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:24,240
No, we just got started.

303
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:27,580
That's right! There's no such thing as 'game over' in life!

304
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:30,460
So that what they've done so far doesn't go to waste,

305
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,790
they convince themselves not to give up.

306
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:37,800
I call this 'dream doping'.

307
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,680
<i>Their dreams, which they believe will come true,</i>

308
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:43,890
turn into a goal they chase.

309
00:19:43,970 --> 00:19:48,520
I have no interest at all in people who deceive themselves like this

310
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:50,480
and get drunk on dreams.

311
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:54,560
<i>If the dream won't come true, it has no meaning.</i>

312
00:19:55,610 --> 00:19:59,440
For this reason, defeat is the turning point of dreams.

313
00:20:00,150 --> 00:20:05,160
What you need is the mental fortitude to accept your powerlessness at that moment.

314
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:09,790
<i>The talent to feel despair.</i>

315
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:12,960
<i>Only by abandoning your dreams</i>

316
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:16,460
<i>will you encounter a path you can see.</i>

317
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:19,340
<i>This path becomes your new potential.</i>

318
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:23,640
To those who continue to fight even when gripped by despair,

319
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:26,550
the power to realize their dreams is granted.

320
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:29,430
Come on, losers.

321
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:33,350
<i>It's your turn to reach the turning point.</i>

322
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:37,270
<i>It was just one step away.</i>

323
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:41,860
<i>If I had received that pass, I could have scored and we would have won!</i>

324
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:45,820
<i>I was completely useless.</i>

325
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:50,790
<i>Even though they got serious, I couldn't stand against them.</i>

326
00:20:50,870 --> 00:20:53,620
<i>These are the facts.</i>

327
00:20:54,370 --> 00:20:55,250
<i>I lost.</i>

328
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,630
<i>What am I...</i>

329
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:03,420
What are we going to do, Isagi?

330
00:21:03,510 --> 00:21:05,800
Yeah, we have to choose someone.

331
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:07,300
Yes.

332
00:21:07,970 --> 00:21:09,930
<i>To defeat Rin,</i>

333
00:21:10,010 --> 00:21:11,930
<i>to get Bachira back,</i>

334
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:15,940
the one I choose...

335
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,650
In that case,

336
00:21:20,020 --> 00:21:21,360
who shall we choose?

337
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:56,790
<i>Teieri Anri's Blue Lock Diary!</i>

338
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:02,670
<i>05:30 wake up, check mail, morning yoga.</i>

339
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:06,880
<i>06:30 wake up Ego-san, clean Ego-san's room.</i>

340
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:09,050
<i>07:30 breakfast.</i>

341
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:13,100
<i>09:00 player health check, meeting with Ego-san.</i>

342
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:15,260
<i>10:00 selection progress check.</i>

343
00:23:15,350 --> 00:23:18,310
<i>10:30 update individual player data.</i>

344
00:23:18,390 --> 00:23:21,060
<i>- 12:30 lunch. - I must not forget the hot water!</i>

345
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:22,900
<i>To win the World Cup,</i>

346
00:23:22,980 --> 00:23:24,450
<i>I'll work in the afternoon too!</i>

347
00:23:24,770 --> 00:23:27,320
<i>13:30 soccer lesson</i>

348
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:28,610
<i>and snack time.</i>

349
00:23:28,690 --> 00:23:31,160
<i>15:00 selection progress check.</i>

350
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,740
<i>15:30 meeting with Ego-san.</i>

351
00:23:33,830 --> 00:23:36,700
<i>18:00 write report for Japan Football Union.</i>

352
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:39,540
<i>19:30 player health check.</i>

353
00:23:39,620 --> 00:23:41,460
<i>20:30 end of work.</i>

354
00:23:41,540 --> 00:23:44,290
<i>21:00 dinner!</i>

355
00:23:46,090 --> 00:23:47,880
I'm exhausted.

356
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:51,930
<i>Anyway, that guy seriously eats nothing but instant noodles.</i>

357
00:23:52,010 --> 00:23:53,970
<i>Is his health okay, I wonder?</i>

358
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:57,520
<i>I should feed him something healthy from time to time.</i>

359
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:58,930
Ego-san!

360
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:02,310
Would you like some stir-fried vegetables as a late-night snack?

361
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:04,770
There's also broccoli salad.

362
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:14,820
Things like this hit the spot sometimes.

363
00:24:14,910 --> 00:24:16,200
Delicious.

364
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:19,450
<i>You screwed up, you idiot!</i>

365
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:22,870
<i>Stay calm, me.</i>

366
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:26,130
I'm glad to hear that.

367
00:24:26,210 --> 00:24:27,960
I wish you a good night.

368
00:24:28,050 --> 00:24:31,260
<i>Everything is to win the World Cup.</i>